    "description": "CenTrio, legally held through CenTrio Energy USA Holdings LLC, owns and operates district heating, cooling and power systems across ten U.S. markets. The Houston-based platform serves commercial, industrial, residential, hospitality, healthcare, research, campus, data-center and government customers through long-lived central plants and thermal networks. The former Enwave U.S. business adopted the CenTrio name in April 2021. Brookfield completed the sale of the platform on July 16, 2021; current sponsor ownership is QIC-managed capital at 75% and Ullico Infrastructure Fund at 25%. QIC's managed interest comprises a disclosed 60% CalPERS/Golden Reef Trust interest and 15% QGIF interest. A July 2026 refinancing reconfirmed QIC and Ullico sponsorship and did not transfer equity. No later equity sale or signed pending ownership transaction was identified through September 1, 2026.",
